    "chunk_text": "constructed by the National Housing Development Authority prior to the year 2012 in and around Colombo is 87, whilst there are two housing schemes in Gampaha, one housing scheme in Jaffna, three housing schemes in Matara, and four housing schemes in Kandy. Most of those housing schemes were built between 1980-2010 and have five or less floors. According to the laws and regulations prevailing at that time, there was no requirement to install elevators. (ii) Elevators have been installed for the two\n\nNational Housing Development Authority for the maintenance of elevators in housing schemes.\n\n213 214\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dd9\n\nEven in respect of the two housing schemes where elevators had been installed, the maintenance activities are scheduled to be handed over to the established Management Corporations once the issuance of deeds is completed. (iv) The Marapalla Resettlement Housing Project was constructed by the Department of Railways. Accordingly, the installation of elevators was also carried out by the said institution. The contracting agency for the Soysapura Phase III Housing Project (30) was the State Engineering Corporation and the installation of elevators was conducted by that institution. (v) No (vi) Not applicable (vii) Staircases have been constructed. (viii) Yes.\n\n\u2022 Slave Island Wekanda Housing Scheme The National Building Research Institute (NBRI) has informed that this housing scheme is in a hazardous condition. \u2022 Nupewela Resettlement Housing Scheme, Matara. This housing scheme was provided to the very low-income earners on a rehabilitation basis in the year 1998. Consisting of two storeys and 34 buildings, the total number of housing units therein is 201. The Department of Buildings has inspected these houses and informed that they are in a condition unfit for occupation.\n\n(b) Not relevant.\n\nNHDA \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dc5\u0db9 \u0db8\u0dc4 \u0db1\u0d9c\u0dad \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dd3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dd4\u0dc5\n\n\u0dc3\u0dc4 \u0dd2\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0db1 \u0db4\u0dd4\u0dad\u0dcf \u0d89\u0dd2\u0db1\u0d9a\u0dad\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0d92\u0d9a\u0d9a:\n\n\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0db1\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dad \u0d94\u0db4\u0dca\u0db4\u0dd4 NHDA\u0b87\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0b95\u0bbe\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1 \u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0b95\u0bb0 \u0bc6\u0bae\u0baa \u0b8e\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0ba8\u0bbe\u0b9f\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb4\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0baf \u0bbe\u0bc0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd"
