    "chunk_size_bytes": 2139,
    "chunk_text": "Moreover, you are frustrating the judges who have served for years in the Judiciary. What happens to those in the minor Judiciary and others? There is a heavy concern among the Judiciary about extending the retirement age of judges. That creates a different issue; that will block their path and deprive many of their right to be appointed to the Bench or to the Superior Courts. Now, High Court Judges will have to wait for their chances and in expectation of being promoted, undue pressure will be brought upon them. This is a way in which the Constitution is being very deliberately violated by the President.\n\n347 348\n\n[\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dca \u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dbd\u0dca \u0db1\u0dca\u0dab\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca \u0db1\u0dca\u200d \u0db8\u0db1\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 ]0\n\nof the judges\u201d, but that is not the issue here. You are waiting until some preferred person becomes eligible to get on to the Bench, to be promoted. So, you are picking and choosing people to be promoted. And by doing that, you are unduly bribing the Judiciary of the country; that is interference with the independent Judiciary.\n\nThen, Madam, I would like to refer to another matter. The Hon. Minister of Justice and National Integration recently said that he is going to bring in amendments to the Prevention of Terrorism Act; \u200d\u0dbb\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dba \u0db4 \u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dd0\u0dc5\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dca\u0db8\u0dda\u0dc0\u0dda \u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dad \u0dc0\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dba \u0d85\u0dd4 \u0dca \u0db4\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dca \u0dc0 \u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dcf \u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dba \u0db4\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dda \u0d85\u0db0\u0dd2 \u0dbb\u0dab \u0d87\u0db8\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf \u0d8a\u0dc0\u0dda \u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dba \u0db4\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u200d\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dcf \u0dc0\u0dda \u0db1\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dba \u0db4\u0dba, \"\u0dca\u0d9f\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca \u0daf\u0dd3\u0dbd\u0dcf .\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dad\u0d9a \u0dd0\u0dca \u0dad\u0dcf \u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dcf\u0dc0 \" \u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dd0\u0da9\u0d9a\u0dca So, once again, you all are going to bring in another Act. I am sure, that would be much more draconian than the existing Act. That is how the Attorney-General\u2019s Department and the Sri Lanka Police behave because they have got used to working under the PTA. Therefore, the investigative power or the efficiency of both the Sri Lanka Police and the Attorney-General\u2019s Department has been retarded by continuing with that draconian legislation."
  },
